    - target: {fileID: 717090539269239051, guid: aacf23fd940d08d419d1dcbc7feb3a70,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: 'Non-metallic (=dielectric) materials, the light that isn''t reflected
        off the surface can enter the material, bounce around inside a bunch of times
        and then exit again if it wasn''t absorbed.





        As with metals,
        if the surface is rough, the light is reflected in different ways. In addition,
        the geometry can mask itself which influences how light is reflected. These
        Microfacets aren''t modelled but instead described statistically with a roughness
        term. Instead of calculating it perfectly, different approximation functions
        exist.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
