    - target: {fileID: 7491782507029020787, guid: aacf23fd940d08d419d1dcbc7feb3a70,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: title
      value: Surface light
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7491782507029020787, guid: aacf23fd940d08d419d1dcbc7feb3a70,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: "SurfaceLight = \r\n\tEmissiveLight + ReflectiveLight\r\n\r\nIn the
        physical world, surfaces can only be seen when they interact with light.
        They can either emit light themselves or reflect light from a different source.\r\nThe
        total light at the surface is the sum of these two.\r\n\r\nWhen just outputting
        the value red, the surface is essentially emitting red light while not interacting
        with the environment light at all."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
