    - target: {fileID: 7564226132419934415, guid: aacf23fd940d08d419d1dcbc7feb3a70,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: title
      value: Combining lights
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 7564226132419934415, guid: aacf23fd940d08d419d1dcbc7feb3a70,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: description
      value: 'Lights can be combined by simply adding their values together. However,
        this can result in values becoming larger than 1.



        The traditional
        method involves using values in such a way that the output is always in the
        range 0...1.



        Meanwhile, more advanced models use realistic brightness
        values and camera exposure models with tone mappers. HDR monitors are also
        able to display more colors and post processing applies bloom to higher values.'
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
